## Develop

```bash
cd {{ service_name }}
uv sync
uv run pytest
SERVICE_MLFLOW_TRACKING_URI=http://localhost:5001 SERVICE_SERVING_ALIAS=dev uv run uvicorn {{ package_name }}.app:app --reload
```

## Ship

1. Register a model named `{{ model_name }}` in the platform registry with the `dev` alias (`make registry-ui` for a port-forward). Dev deploys from `main` and turns ready once `@dev` exists.
2. Image to test: `make promote-image SERVICE={{ service_name }} ENV=test`, then `ENV=prod`. Each opens a PR; CI checks the tag is immutable, exists, and (for prod) has been in test.
3. Model to staging/prod: move the `staging` / `prod` alias. Prod needs a named approver. The API picks up the new version within 30 s.
